马８进７ { [%emt 0:03:46] [%think 21392] [%out 21868] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0]
[%cachewrite 1112] Red's last move (炮四平二) sets up a real threat. My cannon
on h7 acts as the screen, so Red can play 炮二进七 and take the knight on h9.
That knight has nothing defending it, because my rook already left the i-file.
The capture would also be check, with the f9 advisor as the screen. I see two
ways to handle it: 1. **炮8进7, taking the h0 knight first.** Red simply
recaptures with 车一平二. That only trades cannon for knight, and Red's rook
gets developed in the process. 2. **马8进7, moving the knight out.** This is
what I'll play. - Once the knight leaves h9, Red's cannon has nothing to hit
behind my cannon, so the threat is gone. - The knight is developed to a natural
square. - On g7 it guards the centre pawn on e6. That stops a later 炮二进四
followed by 炮二平五, which would take e6 with check. - My h7 cannon can still
take the h0 knight using Red's h2 cannon as the screen. That is only an
exchange offer, since the rook covers h0, but it keeps the option open. - It
also keeps Red from playing 车一平二 directly: a rook on h0 would be hit by my
cannon through the h2 screen. Red has spent two tempi moving that cannon over
and back, so I'm ahead in development. I'd rather develop quickly and keep all
my pieces than simplify early. } 5. 兵七进一 炮２平３ { [%emt 0:04:50]
